{% section tone="dark" %}
## What happens after you get in touch

1. **Send your enquiry:** First, call, email or fill in one of our forms.
2. **We reply:** Then we answer your questions and suggest the best program.
3. **We confirm the details:** After that, we lock in your dates, times and space.
4. **Drum Sing Dance!:** Finally, we arrive with all the drums, so you just bring the group.
{% /section %}

{% section tone="grey" %}
## Rhythm Culture contact FAQs

{% faq %}
{% question title="What’s the best way to contact Rhythm Culture?" %}
For a price, simply use our quick quote form. Otherwise, call 0434 585 992 or email info@rhythmculture.com.au.
{% /question %}

{% question title="What should I include in my enquiry?" %}
First, tell us your dates, location, number of participants and their ages. That way, we can tailor the session and your quote.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Do you travel outside the Sunshine Coast?" %}
Yes. We visit schools, centres and workplaces in Brisbane and across Australia. What’s more, there are no travel fees.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Where are your classes held?" %}
Our weekly classes run on Tuesday nights at Palmwoods Memorial Hall, 1 Main St, Palmwoods.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Do we need our own drums for an incursion?" %}
No. We bring West African drums and percussion for every participant, so there’s nothing extra to hire.
{% /question %}
{% /faq %}
{% /section %}

